# Service principal credentials for unattended runs (--auth spn).
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory and fill in the three values.
# `.env` is read automatically and is git-ignored. Values are never printed --
# only the variable names ever appear in output.
#
# Not needed for interactive use: the default `--auth device` signs in through
# the browser and needs no app registration.
#
# Setup for these three values (needs a tenant admin for step 3):
#   1. Entra ID > App registrations > New registration. Single tenant, no
#      redirect URI. Record the Application (client) ID and Directory (tenant) ID.
#   2. Certificates & secrets > New client secret. Copy it immediately -- it is
#      shown once. Note the expiry; runs break silently on the day it lapses.
#   3. Fabric admin portal > Tenant settings > Developer settings >
#      "Service principals can use Fabric APIs" -> enabled for a security group
#      containing the app.
#   4. The workspace > Manage access > add the app as Contributor.
#
# No API permissions or admin consent are needed on the app itself: Power BI
# governs service principal access through the tenant setting and the workspace
# role, not through Graph scopes.

PBI_TENANT_ID=
PBI_CLIENT_ID=
PBI_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Alternative to the above: paste an access token you already hold and run with
# `--auth token`. Useful for a one-off against a tenant you cannot register an
# app in.
# PBI_ACCESS_TOKEN=
